# The two artefacts a CI drift check regenerates and diffs are pinned to LF.
#
# Same reasoning as the root .gitattributes, which pins the dependency locks
# for the same reason: a generator writes LF, and a checkout under
# `core.autocrlf=true` -- or a commit from a contributor with
# `autocrlf=false` on Windows -- can put CRLF on disk. The gate then
# regenerates, every line differs from the committed bytes, and CI reports
# the whole file as drifted on a tree nobody touched.
#
# That failure is worse here than a phantom diff, because these gates exist
# precisely to answer "did the contract change?". A line-ending mismatch
# answers "yes" every time, and the honest answer stops being legible.
#
# `graphql-codegen.mjs` already writes LF explicitly for the generated
# TypeScript; this covers the SDL, which has no such guard, and makes the
# guarantee a property of the repository rather than of one generator.
#
# Deliberately narrow: only the generated artefacts under frontend/, not a
# blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`. Line-ending policy for the whole tree is a
# decision to take on purpose, not a side effect of adding a codegen step.
schema.graphql        text eol=lf
src/generated/**      text eol=lf
